id: pm-l56d0o
title: "GH-948: version-skewed pm invocations silently rewrite the tracked merge fence during unrelated commands"
description: "Current and supported older pm versions normalize the managed .gitattributes fence differently, and ordinary commands such as pm health invoke that write path. A read-only diagnostic can therefore dirty a tracked file, weaken extension merge protection, and create unrelated diffs solely from PATH or lockfile version skew. Duplicate evidence: all-status exact GH-948 and title searches returned no match; adjacent merge-guidance and gitattributes ownership items are distinct because they do not own cross-version idempotence or the read-only side-effect boundary."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[7]: agent-ux,"area:merge","area:sdk",determinism,read-only,regression,version-skew
created_at: "2026-08-09T14:32:29.084Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-10T15:58:51.053Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-09T15:57:21.544Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-09T15:57:21.544Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "pm health and every read-only bootstrap path leave .gitattributes byte-identical; pm merge install is explicit, deterministic, and preserves compatible managed rules written by newer supported versions; SDK and CLI tests exercise older/newer fence fixtures and dirty-worktree assertions; manual temporary repositories prove health is read-only and explicit installation converges"
parent: pm-dj98
risk: high
confidence: high
reporter: GitHub GH-948
severity: high
environment: Node 26.5.0 Linux; @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.3 through 2026.8.9
repro_steps: "Run npx @unbrained/pm-cli@2026.8.7 health and @2026.8.9 health against the same initialized tracker, restoring .gitattributes between runs; observe opposing tracked diffs."
resolution: Replaced the legacy unversioned merge-driver fence with a v2 fence while preserving legacy public marker constants and added an integration proof that older clients leave the newer fence untouched.
expected_result: Cross-version pm clients must not rewrite or silently downgrade merge-driver configuration they do not understand.
actual_result: "Current clients migrate legacy fences to v2, recognize both generations for audit, and older-version refresh simulation preserves the v2 block byte-for-byte."
affected_version: 2026.8.3-2026.8.9
regression: true
customer_impact: Agents and contributors accumulate unrelated tracked diffs and can accidentally weaken merge safety when local/global pm versions differ.
